[Music]  hi there guys my name's Blanco and this  is a little bit of a return to form for  me I haven't done a gaming impressions  video in a while but a company by the  name of lava boots sent me a free copy  of the early access title wild west and  wizards and yeah so I'm here to take a  look now here's the thing I'm a little  bit biased going into this because well  I love the concept an Old West based  game which we don't get a lot of anymore  mixed with a magic based RPG it sounds  like a good time so without further ado  let's take a look at these uh  spell-casting Cowboys  I love talking about graphics when it  comes to indie titles I really do  because it gives me a chance to talk  about art style and this game's art  style is uh yeah okay I'm not a big fan  of the art direction here I mean I get  it it's an indie title they're like  three people working on this game so  I'll cut them some slack frankly it's  not even so much the environments the  cartoon-like elements in the  environments are you know without  texture and honestly it's fine it  doesn't bother me in fact sometimes it  looks kind of nice my main issues with  the character design I'm not sure which  engine was used to render the characters  within this title they don't really seem  to fit the locales I almost wish they  had gone with less realistically  proportion characters this would help  differentiate this title from others as  well as give the title a sense of world  as it stands now the character models  are quite stiff on the character  selection screen as well as the  inventory screen my character looks like  he's scared to breathe and then every  once in while he'll wipe his face with  his clenched fist who does that on top  of all of that there is a very strange  choice in giving every character  including the NPC's a gun and now I know  this though Old West it's Western and  you know people have guns but come on  everyone  even the doctor like I'm pretty sure if  there were children in this game they'd  have guns too why does the doctor need a  gun yes it's all early access and for  that I deserve some forgiveness as the  developers take time to correct and  correct their vision but yeah it's it's  just odd I'm sure they always look like  this but for now they do and that's what  you'd be paying $15 for lastly I'll talk  about the UI the interface is pretty  generic from things like your health bar  to inventory nothing seems quite  appropriately themed yet I would love  for developers to add some western  themed borders to things like the skill  bar maybe even some different skill  icons I mean the Dodge skill is  literally a stickman but once again  things for the future pretty sure like  once they hire on like an artist or  something I don't know I don't know  you need for that I don't make games now  I know I seem harsh on this tighter than  honestly I think it's warranted not  because the game is bad but because I  think there's genuine potential here and  that shows in the gameplay at the end of  the day gameplay is king  so what we've got here well it's an FPS  one which for the life of me has almost  no business being won but I dig it  you start the game with a revolver and  as you progressed you gain access to  other guns rifles shotguns the works  what's more you were given two spells a  fireball and an ice spell so as you can  imagine the revolver sucks it's the  first gun it's supposed to suck there's  a nice feature within the title that  helps a little bit you can lock on the  targets which you know makes aiming  miles easier then free shooting because  the free shooting is is awful but that's  neither here nor there now you won't  always hit the targets even with the  lock-on this is because the enemies move  which is good but my favorite part of  the enemy AI is the fact they have to  reload as well you don't really see this  a lot I really like this gives you the  opportunity to do things like reload  recast a shield onto yourself or just  unload a clip aside from all of this the  game gives you what most RPGs give you  while it only has one class right now  the devs have made it clear that they  have plans for more there are things  like crafting side quests bounties NPCs  with varying levels of meaningful  dialogue the only thing that really irks  me is that the fact that the map doesn't  really tell you where the hell you are  at any given point and the map is pretty  darn big so not knowing where you are in  the middle of a desert is really bad as  things start to meld into each other the  map that you were given is a brown mass  in yen that that tells me nothing but  overall like I said I like it the fact  the game starts you off almost  immediately the dungeon and lore means  that there is definitely room here for a  dedicated fanbase mmm what more could  you want so all in all I really like  where the game is headed is it for every  RPG seeker no and that's perfect it  knows what it is and it runs with it  while there are a few odds and ends I'd  like to see smoothed out I will  definitely be one to return to this  title to see where the work  you know has gone so with that said if  you'll excuse me I gotta go raid some  bandit camps with my shotgun and book of  curses thanks for watching and stay  perfect  you  [Music]  you

